---

## Scenarios (S0–S9)

| ID | Name | Expected Outcome | Tests |
|----|------|-----------------|-------|
| S0 | Null (no interference) | O2 Null | B1 false attribution |
| S1 | Genuine memory-bandwidth contention | O4 Supported Attribution | Main case |
| S2 | Multiple simultaneous interferers | O4 (OAT: interactions not identified) | Multi-suspect |
| S3 | Workload-phase correlation | O2 Null (randomization breaks correlation) | B1 vs B3 |
| S4 | CPU-frequency pathway | O3 Pathway Violation | C5 detection |
| S5 | Cache and SMT interference | O5 Intervention Effect Only | C5 UNRESOLVED |
| S6 | Carry-over (inadequate washout) | O1 Inconclusive | C8 FAIL |
| S7 | Weak/noisy counters | O1 Inconclusive | C1 FAIL |
| S8 | Nonlinearity/saturation | O4 + extrapolation flag | C7 saturation |
| S9 | Injected exclusion-restriction violation | O3 Pathway Violation | C5 FAIL |

---

## Five-Outcome Policy (O1–O5)

```
O1 Inconclusive       ← Design gate fails, CI ambiguous, or required check fails
O2 Null               ← CI wholly within (−Δ_eff, +Δ_eff)
O3 Pathway Violation  ← Relevant effect + C3/C4/C5 FAIL
O4 Supported Attribution
    Tier 1: both actuators available (C6 PASS)
    Tier 2: single actuator only (C6 UNRESOLVED)
O5 Intervention Effect Only ← Relevant effect + gates pass + ≥1 check UNRESOLVED
```

**UNRESOLVED is never treated as PASS.**

